Falsifies `usb::verification::two_interfaces_are_walked_as_two`.

The defect: an interface descriptor opens a candidate when it is a boot keyboard and leaves the
previous one open when it is not, so an endpoint of a later mouse or vendor interface is read as
the keyboard's. The fully symbolic walk harness cannot see it, because it never reaches a second
interface.

Expected to fail: the harness's "an endpoint of the boot interface it names" assertion.

diff --git a/crates/universal_serial_bus/src/descriptor.rs b/crates/universal_serial_bus/src/descriptor.rs
--- a/crates/universal_serial_bus/src/descriptor.rs
+++ b/crates/universal_serial_bus/src/descriptor.rs
@@ -288,3 +288,5 @@
                     && d[7] == PROTOCOL_KEYBOARD;
-                candidate = is_boot_keyboard.then_some(d[2]);
+                if is_boot_keyboard {
+                    candidate = Some(d[2]);
+                }
             }
